meta {
  name: Change Cluster Scope
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/clusters/{{clusterId}}/scope
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Dev-User-ID: {{devUserId}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "new_scope": "public",
    "reason": "Promoting to public catalogue per programme owner approval ticket SAIDKICK-42."
  }
}

docs {
  Promotes or demotes a cluster between public and an org-scoped visibility. PlatformAdmin only.

  Validation / behaviour:
    1. Authentication required; PlatformAdmin role enforced — ClusterAdmin gets 403.
    2. Parse cluster ID — 404 if not found.
    3. reason field is required (any non-empty string).
    4. new_scope must be "public", "org", or "restricted" — 422 on invalid value.
       For org/restricted, owning_org_id is also required.
    5. No-op check: 409 if new_scope already matches the current scope.
    6. Update cluster row (scope + owning_organization_id) in a transaction.
    7. Write cluster.scope_changed to audit_logs with before/after scope and reason.

  Responses:
    200 OK            — updated cluster object
    401 unauthorized  — unauthenticated
    403 forbidden     — caller is not PlatformAdmin
    404 not_found     — cluster not found
    409 no_op         — cluster is already in that scope
    422 validation_failed — reason missing or new_scope format invalid
}
